    "awards": [],
    "insight": {
      "what": "This was a really fun one. MẢNH — a Vietnamese tradition-inspired fashion brand — reached out and said: “We have this very cool campaign coming up, and we want to show how we make it.”",
      "problem": "Working with T R A G, founder of MẢNH, I got to understand the mind behind the clothes, her character, and the stories that shape her artistic personality. “Fashion should be experimental and distinct. I hope whoever wears my work finds comfort in it as they finally step out of their fashion comfort zone,” she told me. For this campaign, T R A G wrote and drew a one-shot comic — her own vision and take on the folklore “Tấm Cám,” an ancient story of two stepsisters filled with karma and the clash between good and evil. MẢNH clothing would be a representation of that.",
      "audience": "I led the video production. Just showing “how we make it” wasn’t enough. I wanted to go beyond a simple behind-the-scenes piece and instead create a work-in-progress visualization of an evolving idea. The goal was to let the audience feel what it’s like to be “there” on set as the concept grows from a thought, to notes, to artworks, and finally to fashion pieces being worn.",
      "process": "The big idea: “To Create is to Experience without Boundaries.” The concept sits at the intersection of art and tech, between cultural texts and contemporary media, between traditional craftsmanship and experimental execution, between storytelling and fashion. All of that comes together to represent one word: creativity.",
      "result": "It was a deliberate creative choice to shoot this promo entirely on iPhone 17 Pro Max. With the iPhone, we could achieve angles and movements that would normally take much more setup with a standard camera. And that “iPhone” feel, it's just different."
    },
    "media": [
